Package: dtiiv
Title: Distributional Tendency Intrinsic Instrumental Variables
Version: 0.1.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("Ratbek", "Dzhumashev", email = "ratbek.dzhumashev@monash.edu", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Ainura", "Tursunalieva", email = "ainura.tursunalieva@data61.csiro.au", role = "aut"))
Description: Estimates the slope of an endogenous regressor in a linear model
    without an external instrument. The regressor is rotated against the
    residual so that, at the true slope, its exogenous component and the
    error satisfy distributional tendency conditions: the variance tendency,
    mean tendencies E[u h(s)] = 0, and error-side tendencies E[s a(u)] = 0.
    These conditions use the skewness and kurtosis of the data. The package
    computes identification-robust confidence sets by inverting a
    cluster-robust score test with first-step corrections and Hotelling-type
    critical values, continuously updated GMM estimates with J tests, and the
    roots of the variance tendency.
